Microduck procedural vocalisations
Source: https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck
Revision: 6cdfdaad21bed25e01b450c0dd4e0aee0ae19fde
Upstream license: Apache-2.0 (included as LICENSE).

These WAV assets use the unmodified official Rust sounds recipes in
sounds/src/{personality,rng,synth,voices}.rs, bank version 5, seed 100,
variant 0. The upstream sounds crate credits apirrone/microduck_sounds
as the original Python implementation.

Radxa Duck renders the six one-shot voices offline, converts using the
upstream synth::to_i16 function, and duplicates the mono samples into both
48 kHz PCM16 channels for Pollen HAT playback. No pitch, amplitude or timing
adjustments are applied. File hashes and durations are in manifest.json.
